<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Nystad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1721</span> · Also known as Peace of Nystad · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Nystad was the peace agreement of 1721 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Sweden ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingria">Ingria</a> and part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a> to Russia. The treaty marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> as a great power and the emergence of Russia, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>, as the dominant power of the Baltic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad.jpg" alt="Treaty of Nystad" width="247" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mix321 at Polish Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NystatIngria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
